MOTION
The original three clips remain: spikes and iris each activate over 24 frames
at 24 fps (one second); the pendulum swings over 24 frames at 12 fps (a two-second
loop). The combined review plays the activations forward/back beside one
pendulum cycle. Individual MP4s use the runtime frame rates. Extra GIF holds
are inspection conveniences. The vent, bridge and crusher have still states
and retained parametric source, matching the original delivered scope.

REGISTRATION
Default canvas: 1536 x 1536, common root [768, 1220], density 440 pixels/metre.
Crusher canvas: 1536 x 1792, root [768, 1420]. Its 200-pixel padding translation
does not change world scale. Orthographic elevation 35.2643897 degrees and
azimuth 45 degrees; XZ ground, Y up. No state is fitted or resized independently.
RGBA8, straight alpha. New bounds and collision require engine-side review.

ART AND SOURCE
Untouched new image-generation masters supply shaped oak, forged steel, bronze
and chipped stone. Exact prompts, separated layers, clipping meshes and Python
rig source are included. The original art and hero reference remain unchanged.
Spikes retain rigid pyramid geometry while translating through a fixed deck.
Iris leaves keep fixed pivots. Pendulum shaft, neck and blade share one bearing.
Bridge upper/underside materials share its true hinge. The crusher uses freshly
illustrated isometric volumes registered by their chain eyes; fixed guide lips
occlude the carriage, and fractional UV clipping reels chains without stretching
links. Steam uses a fresh, simple three-tone master at the fixed outlet.
No animation frame was independently regenerated. No alpha threshold or added
noise/grain filter is applied. The original SVG source is superseded by the new
master/layer/mesh/Python source; asset, state and clip IDs remain unchanged.
Painted volumes and recesses are artistic fixed-view imagery, not fully
calibrated, relightable 3D meshes. Exact anchors are not collision geometry.

