SELF-CONTAINED REBUILD
Install Python 3, Pillow and NumPy; install ffmpeg on PATH for review movies.
The included requirements.txt records the versions used for this release.
From the extracted pack root, run:
  python source/build_hazards.py
  python source/package_proof.py
The scripts also accept absolute script paths from another working directory.
The proof generator uses bundled historical before-images under
source/reference_before/; they are comparison references, not replacement art.
A redistributable DejaVu font and its license are bundled in source/fonts/,
with a Pillow default-font fallback. No old workspace or Linux font path is
required. Context diagrams are regenerated by source/context_proofs.py.
A source-only copy was rebuilt from an unrelated working directory; all
18 state PNGs and 72 runtime frame PNGs matched the release byte-for-byte.

SAFETY AND INTEGRATION
Presentation art only. These files define no damage window, trigger, safe state,
traversal rule, cooldown, collision or real-world mechanical suitability.
A broken/jammed image must not be read as a harmless gameplay state. No game
repository was modified; engine import, relighting, runtime atlases, collision
and performance validation remain integration work.
